.TH VC4INFER 1 "25 November 2026" "vc4infer 1.2.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vc4infer \- run fixed-shape fp32 ONNX models on the VideoCore IV QPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc4infer
[\fB\-\-backend\fR \fImanaged\fR|\fIdirect\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B vc4infer \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vc4infer
executes an ONNX graph on the twelve QPUs of a Raspberry Pi VideoCore IV and
returns its outputs.  Every floating-point operator runs on the QPUs; there is
no CPU arithmetic fallback, so an operator, shape or attribute outside the
supported set raises and names itself instead of running slowly.
.PP
The default backend is
.BR managed :
an unprivileged client that talks to
.BR vc4d (8)
over a socket.  The
.B direct
backend maps the arena itself, needs root and exists for measurement and the
low-level test suite.
.PP
A model can be run straight from ONNX, or built once into a
.I .vc4x
engine artifact that freezes the optimiser passes, the packed weight panels,
the kernel blobs and both the allocation and execution plans.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS run \fIMODEL\fR
Run one inference.  For a detector the outputs are decoded to boxes; for other
graphs they are printed as tensors.
.TP
.B \-\-input \fIPATH\fR
An image (jpg, png), a
.I .npy
tensor or a
.I .csv
file.  Without it the input is random, which is only useful for timing.
.TP
.B \-\-imgsz \fIN\fR
Letterbox size for an image input.  It must match the model's input.
.TP
.B \-\-conf \fIF\fR
Confidence threshold (default 0.25).
.TP
.B \-\-iou \fIF\fR
NMS IoU threshold (default 0.45).
.TP
.B \-\-max-det \fIN\fR
Maximum detections kept (default 300).
.TP
.B \-\-classes \fIPATH\fR
One class name per line; defaults to COCO-80.
.TP
.B \-\-out \fIPATH\fR
Annotated image path (default
.IR input_vc4infer.jpg ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-save
Do not write an annotated image.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON document instead of a table.
.TP
.B \-\-save-json \fIPATH\fR
Also write the JSON document to this path.
.SS bench \fIMODEL\fR
Time a model end to end and report wall time, FPS, launches, QPU duty and the
partition of time between the QPU, the host and the launch path.
.TP
.B \-\-imgsz \fIN\fR
Input size, validated against the model.
.TP
.B \-\-reps \fIN\fR
Timed runs (default 3).
.TP
.B \-\-input \fIPATH\fR
A real input instead of random data.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SS nodes \fIMODEL\fR
Static report: what each node is, which backend would run it, and what is
refused, by name.  The authoritative answer comes from
.BR run ;
this command is the one to try first on an unfamiliar graph.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
List every node with its status, backend and reason.
.TP
.B \-\-mode {strict,hybrid}
Which policy the report describes (default hybrid for a report, strict for
execution).
.TP
.B \-\-host-policy {device,structural,any}
Under hybrid: what the host may do.  \fIdevice\fR forbids runtime host compute,
\fIstructural\fR allows metadata and control, \fIany\fR also runs unwritten
numeric operators.
.SS util \fIMODEL\fR
Device-invariant utilisation accounting: what share of the frame is QPU
arithmetic, what moved over the wire, and how many launches each class needs.
.TP
.B \-\-imgsz \fIN\fR
Input size.
.TP
.B \-\-reps \fIN\fR
Timed runs (default 3).
.TP
.B \-\-input \fIPATH\fR
A real input instead of random data.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SS selftest
Run the four reference models shipped in
.IR /usr/share/vc4infer/models ,
compare every output against its recorded reference and print the maximum
absolute and relative difference.  Exit status 1 when any element is over
tolerance, 8 when the model files are not the packaged ones.
.TP
.B \-\-models \fIDIR\fR
Model directory (default
.IR /usr/share/vc4infer/models ).
.SS build \fIMODEL\fR
Convert a model into a
.I .vc4x
engine artifact.  This is the deployable form: the optimiser runs once, the
weight panels are packed, the kernel blobs are generated and hashed, and the
allocation and execution plans are frozen.  The result loads in about half a
second instead of three to four, and refuses by name when it is paired with a
different engine, board or kernel ABI.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-out \fIPATH\fR
Output artifact (default
.IR model.vc4x ).
.TP
.B \-\-opt \fISPEC\fR
Optimiser passes baked in: \fIall\fR (default), \fInone\fR, or a comma-separated
list such as \fIepilogue,layout\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-imgsz \fIN\fR
Export size for a
.I .pt
input (default 640), recorded in the artifact.
.TP
.B \-\-opset \fIN\fR
Export opset for a
.I .pt
input (default 17), recorded.
.TP
.B \-\-no-embed-graph
Reference an adjacent
.I .onnx
instead of embedding the graph in the artifact.
.TP
.B \-\-no-embed-kernels
Record kernel blob names and hashes only; the loader then needs the cache to
hold them.
.TP
.B \-\-arena-mb \fIN\fR
Client arena to plan against (default: what the daemon serves).
.SS verify \fIARTIFACT\fR
Check every section and every key of a
.I .vc4x
against this engine, board and kernel ABI, without running it.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-backend {managed,direct}
Execution backend (default managed).  The same choice can be made with
.BR VC4INFER_BACKEND .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version, the engine API version and the backend and socket in
use, then exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Usage, for the command as a whole or after a command name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VC4_OPT
Optimiser passes for the ONNX path, used when
.B \-\-opt
is not given: empty or \fInone\fR runs the graph unfolded, \fIall\fR runs every
pass, or a comma-separated list.  Folded graphs need fewer launches, so an
unset variable measures the slow path.
.TP
.B VC4_CPLAN, VC4_NO_CPLAN
Enable or disable the frozen execution plan (default enabled).
.B VC4_NO_CPLAN=1
is the A/B control.
.TP
.B VC4_NO_MEM_PLAN
Set to 1 to size the pool with the old walk instead of the plan-time
allocator, for comparison.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_BACKEND
\fImanaged\fR or \fIdirect\fR, same as
.BR \-\-backend .
.TP
.B VC4INFER_DAEMON
1 selects the daemon backend; 0 is the direct-root path used by the low-level
test suite.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_LIB
Path to
.IR libvc4infer.so ;
a checkout's build wins over the installed library.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_CACHE
Kernel blob cache directory (default
.IR ~/.cache/vc4infer/kcache ).
.TP
.B VC4INFER_KGEN
Path to the kernel generator, for a tree that is not installed.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_ARENA_MB
Arena to request from the daemon, in MiB.
.TP
.B VC4_POOL_RESERVE_MB
Extra pool slack for graphs whose temporary need the estimate understates.
.TP
.B VC4D_SOCKET
Daemon socket (default
.IR /run/vc4d.sock ).
.TP
.B VC4INFER_MODELS
Reference model directory for
.BR selftest .
.TP
.B VC4INFER_NO_BATCH
1 disables batched launch submission, for the A/B comparison.
.TP
.B VC4INFER_PROF
1 enables the launch-path profiler and per-node statistics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/vc4d.sock
the default daemon socket
.TP
.I /usr/share/vc4infer/models
the reference models and their checksums
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vc4infer/kcache
generated kernel blobs, keyed by name and hashed
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a shipped detector on an image:
.PP
.nf
.RS
vc4infer run /usr/share/vc4infer/models/yolov8n_160.onnx \\
    --imgsz 160 --input photo.jpg
.RE
.fi
.PP
Build, verify and use an artifact of your own model:
.PP
.nf
.RS
VC4_OPT=all vc4infer build model.onnx \-o model.vc4x
vc4infer verify model.vc4x
vc4infer run model.vc4x --imgsz 160 --input photo.jpg \\
    --classes names.txt
.RE
.fi
.PP
Check the four reference models:
.PP
.nf
.RS
vc4infer selftest
.RE
.fi
.PP
Time a shipped detector and see what a graph is made of:
.PP
.nf
.RS
vc4infer bench /usr/share/vc4infer/models/yolov8n_160.onnx \\
    --imgsz 160 --reps 5
vc4infer nodes model.onnx -v
.RE
.fi
.PP
In a source checkout,
.I tools/demo.sh
runs the five steps of the second example above in one command and prints the
output of each.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
a reference model is over tolerance, or a run failed
.TP
.B 2
usage error: bad arguments, a missing file, a model and input that disagree
.TP
.B 3
an operator, shape or attribute is unsupported, or the arena is exhausted
.TP
.B 4
host debt under the device policy
.TP
.B 6
control flow that the host-scheduled executor cannot run
.TP
.B 8
the shipped model files are not the packaged ones
.SH NOTES
The QPU is a single resource: run one client at a time.  The daemon serialises
launches, so a second client does not corrupt the first, but two timed runs at
once measure each other.
.PP
An artifact is tied to the engine that built it: a package upgrade invalidates
it, and
.B verify
says so rather than running it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vc4d (8),
.BR vc4\-query (1),
.BR vc4\-smi (1),
.BR vc4top (1).
.PP
Documentation under
.IR /usr/share/doc/vc4infer .
